#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Data Template"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "The Cacti Data Template this definition ranks. The portable template hash is stored, so the definition survives export/import between installs. The count shows how many Data Sources currently use each template."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Display Name"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "A friendly name shown in the TopX dashboards. Leave blank to use the Data Template name."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Metric Expression"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "How the RRD data source fields are combined, e.g. \"cpu=cpu\" (single field), \"traffic_in+traffic_out\" (sum) or \"hdd_total%hdd_used\" (percentage). Append \"/N\" to divide a single field by a constant so the chart and ranking use the scaled value, e.g. \"uptime=uptime/8640000\" to convert SNMP uptime timeticks to days."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Metric Label"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "A short label for what is measured, e.g. \"Utilization\", \"Bits\". Used for the chart value axis."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Range Direction"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Whether a higher value is the more significant one (increasing, e.g. CPU/traffic) or a lower value is (decreasing, e.g. free disk space or uptime headroom). Drives the default ranking sense and threshold colouring."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Default Sort"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "The default sort direction applied when this source is first opened."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Ascending"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Descending"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Display Format"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "How a computed value is formatted for display. \"Static Unit\" rounds to the Decimal Places and appends a single, fixed Display Unit (e.g. \"%\", \"days\"). \"Division by Unit Ladder\" steps a value through a ladder of divisors and units, showing it in the largest unit whose divided value is at least one (e.g. bits → Kbit → Mbit)."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Division by Unit Ladder"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Static Unit"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Decimal Places"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "How many decimal places the displayed value is rounded to. \"Auto\" uses two places. Applies to both Display Formats."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Display Unit(s)"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "The unit shown after the value. For \"Static Unit\" a single label such as \"%\" or \"days\". For \"Division by Unit Ladder\" a slash-delimited list of unit names, from smallest to largest, paired position-for-position with the Display Unit Ladder divisors (e.g. \"bit/Kbit/Mbit/Gbit\")."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Display Unit Ladder"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Only used by \"Division by Unit Ladder\". A slash-delimited list of divisors, one per unit in Display Unit(s) and in the same order, from smallest to largest (e.g. units \"bit/Kbit/Mbit\" with divisors \"1/1000/1000000\", or binary \"1/1024/1048576\"). The value is shown in the largest unit whose divided result is at least one."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Value System"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "The numbering system used when auto-scaling unsupported values."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Normal Threshold"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Optional. The upper bound of the healthy band. Leave blank to disable threshold colouring."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Warning Threshold"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Optional. Values at or beyond this (at or below, for decreasing ranges) are shown in the warning colour."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Alert Threshold"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Optional. Values at or beyond this (at or below, for decreasing ranges) are shown in the alert colour."
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "Chart Label Pattern"
msgstr ""

#: topx_sources.php
msgid "How each ranked item is named on the chart, using |token| substitution: |host_description|, |host_hostname|, |host_id| and |query_<field>| (e.g. |query_ifName|). Example: \"|host_description| - |query_ifName|\". Leave blank to derive the label from the Data Source name."
msgstr ""

